>> title: Chinese Chicken Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: chicken, cabbage, sesame, wonton, salad
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: chinese chicken salad, oriental chicken salad, asian chicken salad, chopped chicken salad, brentwood chinese chicken, crispy wonton salad, sesame chicken salad
>> pairs-with: goma-dare, miso-ginger-dressing
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> slack: narrow — the wonton strips are crisp for about twenty minutes after the dressing hits them and are wet cardboard by the hour
>> step.1: poach 15 min, cool in the liquid
>> step.2: fry 2 min, drain hard
>> step.3: shred by hand
>> step.4: slice fine
>> step.5: toss

Poach @chicken breasts{1%lb}(450 g) with @ginger{3%slices}, @scallion{1}(halved) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} in a #saucepan{} of barely trembling water for ~poach{15%min}, then take the pan off the heat and ~cool{20%min} the breasts in their own liquid.

Fry @wonton wrappers{8}(stacked and cut in 1/4-in ribbons) in @neutral oil{1%cup}(240 mL) in a #skillet{} for ~fry{2%min}, a handful at a time, and drain them on paper.

Shred @&(~2)poached chicken{} along the grain, by hand, into pieces about the width of a pencil.

Slice @napa cabbage{4%cups}(shredded fine), @romaine{2%cups}(shredded fine), @carrot{1%large}(julienned), @scallions{3}(on a long bias) and @cilantro{1/2%cup}(leaves and thin stems).

Toss @&(~1)shredded vegetables{} with @&(~2)chicken{}, @goma dare{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @toasted almonds{1/3%cup}(sliced) and @toasted sesame seeds{1%Tbs}, then throw @&(~3)fried wontons{} over the top.

A spoonful of water into the dressing first: it wants to be looser here. Wontons on top and never tossed through.
